id: pm-gh1563
title: "GH-1563: preserve later peer edits during bulk checkpoint rollback"
description: "External report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1563. Revalidate the reported 2026.10.23 behavior against the checkout before implementation."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: github-intake,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-23T23:21:32.081Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T00:15:24.332Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T00:15:23.577Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-24T00:15:23.577Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Rollback reverses only successful batch effects; unrelated peer metadata and annotations remain; drift on batch-modified fields refuses without writes; failed forward rows are never restored; close-many uses the same protection
parent: pm-lf6s
risk: high
confidence: 95
resolution: "Checkpoint schema2 binds committed target-item writes to immutable history; rollback verifies the live item and field postimages under the normal fenced mutation lock, reverses only those effects, preserves unrelated peer context, skips absent or already-reversed effects, and refuses legacy or drifted recovery without implicit force."
expected_result: Undo successful bulk effects while preserving later peer edits and truthful conflict/no-effect receipts across SDK and CLI.
actual_result: "Three pre-fix controls failed at the intended loss/false-success boundaries. Final focused144 tests, linked20 tests, packed npm/Bun acceptance and strict typecheck pass. Full local coverage failures were repaired and rechecked; final hosted coverage remains mandatory before merge."
